Curriculum
We have reviewed and introduced a new curriculum for our children, which is based upon the key elements that we feel this generation of children need to learn about in order to survive and be successful in the future.
So that our children are suitably equipped to be successful in the future, we ensure that we are teaching our children the knowledge and skills they need:
Two key challenges we feel this generation of children have to face in the future and need to be prepared for are:
for learning;
for living;
for work;
for life.
1. Ensuring the wellbeing of individuals
This is due to the increase in the following issues on a local, national and global scale:
Health issues;
Mental Health issues;
Social issues;
2. Ensuring we live in a sustainable environment
This is to understand the following issues on a local, national and global scale:
Pollution;
Waste & recycling;
Energy use;
Changes in our climate;
Protection of endangered habitats & species.
Our Curriculum rationale is based around three key elements:
Looking after ourselves Looking after each other
Looking after our planet
